   "text": {
    "L1": "The Earth is a ball, and the Sun shines on it like a torch.",
    "L2": "The half facing the Sun has day; the half turned away has night.",
    "L3": "The Earth keeps spinning on its axis, making one full turn in about 24 hours.",
    "L4": "As the Earth turns, a place moves from dark into light, then from light into dark.",
    "L5": "The Sun seems to rise in the east and set in the west because the Earth spins from west to east.",
    "L6": "At night the Sun does not hide behind mountains or go around the Earth; our side has turned away.",
    "L7": "When it is day in India, the other side of Earth can have night, while nearby Dubai differs by only a little time.",
    "L8": "So what causes day and night? Tap the best explanation."
   },
